internal/store/store.go:422-425

The MigrateSetOwner comment reads:

  // NewIsEmpty matches missing/null keys but not an empty string,
  // so auth-disabled records (owner=="") are intentionally left alone.

Two imprecisions:

1. 'missing/null keys' conflates two distinct concepts: a missing key (key absent from payload) and a null value (key present with null). Qdrant's is_empty matches both, but they are different states. More importantly, is_empty also matches empty arrays ([]) — the comment omits this third case.

2. For the owner keyword field specifically the behavior described is correct: is_empty will not match owner="". But a future reader maintaining a different field (e.g., an array field) who looks at this comment as a reference for is_empty semantics will be misled.

Suggested fix:
  // NewIsEmpty matches absent keys, null values, and empty arrays — but NOT an
  // empty string, so auth-disabled records (owner=="") are intentionally skipped.

